      "writtenOn": "2024-08-15T17:39:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I do withdraw my comment about use of the `unsafe` keyword. I agree that the sheer existence of a `\u0026mut [u8]` here _theoretically_ guarantees safety, in that cxx should not allow the creation of a `\u0026mut [u8]` to uninitialized data. If cxx does allow the creation of such a reference, and the referent is uninitialized, that\u0027s a known limitation of cxx.\n\nBut... I still feel uncomfortable about use of the word `SAFETY` here because that sort of comment is normally associated with the preconditions of calling a Rust `unsafe` function. So I think I\u0027m fine with it if you remove that word, as I think it just confused me and will probably confuse others similarly.",
      "parentUuid": "ebcc8c1e_be0f436e",
      "revId": "cec9aeb4b6f567a9c1f975c3442dffe42cfd4d2f",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
